    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d571">

                <pb facs="0640" n="628" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg628"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00114 European War 1939/3861: Airgram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-05-28T13:00:00-03:00">May 28, 1943—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 4—5 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–1045. Aranha tells me that the Brazilian Government will receive the prisoners
                    under the conditions set out in the Department’s instruction No. 4405 of May 1,
                    1943. He suggested that I send a representative to talk about details to Fraga
                    de Castro.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d571-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d571-f1" n="30" xml:id="d571-f1-content">
                <p>Edgar Fraga de Castro, official of the Ministry for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
